## Why This Is Asked
This tests formulating a DP over partitions with a subarray-internal metric.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP
- Prefix sums
- Reconstruction pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
// DP skeleton
function maxValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i]+A[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const cut = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1;i<=n;i++) {
     for (let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++) {
        let maxVal = -Infinity; let bestP = -1; let curMax = -Infinity;
        for (let p=i-1; p>=t-1; p--) {
           curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[p]);
           const val = dp[p][t-1] + (pref[i]-pref[p]) - curMax;
           if (val>maxVal) { maxVal=val; bestP=p; }
        }
        dp[i][t] = maxVal; cut[i][t] = bestP;
     }
  }
  return {value: dp[n][k], cuts: cut};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What is the time complexity and how would you optimize to O(nk) with a deque?
- How would you reconstruct the exact subarray endpoints?

## Why This Is Asked
Combinatorial DP with partitioning; tests clear recurrence and reconstruction, common in interviews. 

## Key Concepts
- dp[i][t] = min over p of dp[p][t-1] + max(A[p..i-1]);
- Track parent to reconstruct partition points; iterate i and t in increasing order.

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1] = Math.max(...A.slice(0,i));
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      let curMax = -Infinity;
      for(let p=i-1; p>=t-1; p--){
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[p]);
        const cand = dp[p][t-1] + curMax;
        if(cand < dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = cand; par[i][t] = p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {cost: dp[n][k], par};
}
```

